    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11406" root="خلق" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَلَائِقُ</span></b>  [pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَلِيقَةٌ</span>]. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الخَلَائِقُ</span> <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَمَائِرُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَآءِ</span>, i. e. <i>Four large and smooth masses of stone
at the head of the well, upon which the drawer of
the water stands.</i> (TA.) Accord. to Ibn-'Abbád,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَوْضٌ بَادِى الخَلَائِقِ</span> means [<i>A watering-trough
of which</i>] <i>the</i> [<i>stones termed</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَصَائِب</span> [<i>appear</i>].
(JK, TA. [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَصِيبَةٌ</span>.])

